Benjamin Scott-Hopkins wrote:
>
> I think I know how prayer works (read the FAQ, searched here, &c.) but
> I want to make sure about a few things. Essentially, all that matters
> (if you want favors) is positive luck and positive alignment, right?

And the timeout.

> Neither have to be _super_ high, do they?

Alignment just needs to be positive.  Timeout just needs to be zero.
For luck, the higher your luck the better the stuff that happens on
the average.

> 1. I'm hogging the minetown altar, with plenty of food. I'm n400.
> (resting) untill something comes up, and then I whack it and sac it.
> If I want to maximaize the cool things (glows, books, &c.) should I
> pray the instant that I feel reconciled? Or should I wait until I get
> some more clovers?

Depends on your goal.  For getting artifact gifts, keep saccing and
never pray.  For intrinsics and other benefits pray as soon as you
feel reconciled.

> 2. Should I spend a long time sacrificing to my god on the way down
> the mine (ie before I have the luckstone) or should I wait until I
> come back up with it, and bless it, too?

Judgement call.  I'd go with getting a gift weapon first, then
beeline down to the stone, then come back and bless it.

> 3. As a chaotic, is it worthwhile to kill and sacrifice members of my
> own race? You get an Annoying Demon, I know, but also (I believe) and
> significant align bonus, are there other penalties than just the
> demon?

If the demon is here friendly it will never be deeper hostile.

> Finally, 4. Does it matter what level I am when I start saccing? I
> want maximal gifts, and minimal chance of being crowned. I know you
> can't convert altars until level 3, and of course you can't really
> kill big monsters at too low a level, but aside from that, how does
> level matter?

For that combination of goals you mostly want to avoid prayer after
you get the luckstone.  But being crowned isn't that big a problem.
Make sure you wield a regular long sword every time you pray until you
get crowned of course.  More judgement calls.  I like to sac until I
have "a few" gift weapons then switch to prayer until I get crowned to
ensure I have a good-enough weapon in addition when I get crowned.

